    "q-180980": {
      "dom_id": "step-q180980",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "If $10=y+6$, then $y=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\ny+6=10\n$$\n\nTo isolate $y$, we need to perform the *opposite* of adding $6$ to $y$, which is *subtracting* $6$ from $y.$ Remember to perform the same operation on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+6 & =10 \\\\ y+6-6 & =10-6 \\\\ y+0 & =4 \\\\ y & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
