      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "If $y-3=5.5$, then $y=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "To isolate $y$, we need to perform the *opposite* of subtracting $3$ from $y$, which is *adding* $3$ to $y.$ Remember to perform the same operation on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-3 & =5.5 \\\\ y-3+3 & =5.5+3 \\\\ y+0 & =8.5 \\\\ y & =8.5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
