    "q-101696": {
      "dom_id": "step-q101696",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Solve the equation $-\\frac{3}{2}=d-\\frac{5}{7}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's swap the left and right-hand sides so that the variable is on the left-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2} & =d-\\frac{5}{7} \\\\ d-\\frac{5}{7} & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo isolate $d$, we need to perform the *opposite* of subtracting $\\frac{5}{7}$ from $d$, which is *adding* $\\frac{5}{7}$ to $d.$ Remember to perform the same operation on the right-hand side.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}d-\\frac{5}{7} & =-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ d-\\frac{5}{7}+(\\frac{5}{7}) & =-\\frac{3}{2}+(\\frac{5}{7}) \\\\ d+0 & =-\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{5}{7} \\\\ d & =\\frac{-3\\cdot 7+5\\cdot 2}{14} \\\\ d & =-\\frac{11}{14}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
